      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "--> You could also do this by using an ImageStream with \n    an infrastructure as code YAML file\n\n\n--> Here, we have an example in your text material that shows\n   how the different annotations and labels can be used with\n   an ImageStream to let OpenShift know that a particular \n   image is available to be used within OpenShift AI as \n   a Workbench Image",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> You could also do this by using an ImageStream with \n    an infrastructure as code YAML file\n\n\n--> Here, we have an example in your text material that shows\n   how the different annotations and labels can be used with\n   an ImageStream to let OpenShift know that a particular \n   image is available to be used within OpenShift AI as \n   a Workbench Image",
